From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mpereiraesaa <manuelpereiralds@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:59:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: TLS root certificates from curl's 2026-10-20 extract of
 Mozilla's store

prospero-win 404cac6 (#728), after the v0.2.0 PC5 builds on, picked onto
PC5's patches.

Bumped for v0.3.0 as the release checklist asks: cacert-2026-10-20.pem, 118 roots. GnuTLS 3.8.13 and nettle 3.10.2 are still their newest releases.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md        | 2 +-
 tests/test_package_release.py | 2 +-
 tools/build_tls_ps5.sh        | 4 ++--
 3 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md b/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md
index 0df672b..7f8681d 100644
--- a/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md
+++ b/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md
@@ -992,7 +992,7 @@ see, so it stayed empty. Patch 0878 reads `share/wine/ca-certificates.crt`
 beside the runtime first, found from `crypt32.prx`'s own path with
 `dladdr`, and logs an error if it is not there. The bundle is Mozilla's
 root store as curl publishes it, a dated file pinned by URL and SHA-256 in
-`build_tls_ps5.sh` (`cacert-2026-09-25.pem`, 121 roots), so a release
+`build_tls_ps5.sh` (`cacert-2026-10-20.pem`, 118 roots), so a release
 carries the same roots whoever builds it; `PROSPERO_CA_BUNDLE` names
 another, and `SOURCES.txt` then records only its SHA-256. The pinned bundle
 ages with Mozilla's store (roots are added and withdrawn a few times a
diff --git a/tests/test_package_release.py b/tests/test_package_release.py
index f39c1fa..92588a1 100644
--- a/tests/test_package_release.py
+++ b/tests/test_package_release.py
@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@ def main() -> int:
                          "nettle 3.10.2 (libgnutls.prx)  https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/nettle/nettle-3.10.2.tar.gz",
                          "SHA-256 fe9ff51cb1f2abb5e65a6b8c10a92da0ab5ab6eaf26e7fc2b675c45f1fb519b5",
                          "Root certificates (share/wine/ca-certificates.crt)  the builder's own bundle,"
-                         " not curl's cacert-2026-09-25.pem",
+                         " not curl's cacert-2026-10-20.pem",
                          f"SHA-256 {hashlib.sha256(b'roots').hexdigest()}"):
             assert expected in sources, (expected, sources)
         assert "https://curl.se/ca/" not in sources
diff --git a/tools/build_tls_ps5.sh b/tools/build_tls_ps5.sh
index 49dd62b..088c4f9 100755
--- a/tools/build_tls_ps5.sh
+++ b/tools/build_tls_ps5.sh
@@ -31,8 +31,8 @@ GNUTLS_SHA256=ffed8ec1bf09c2426d4f14aae377de4753b53e537d685e604e99a8b16ca9c97e
 GNUTLS_URL=https://www.gnupg.org/ftp/gcrypt/gnutls/v3.8/gnutls-$GNUTLS_VERSION.tar.xz
 # Mozilla's root store, extracted by curl's mk-ca-bundle (MPL-2.0); the
 # dated files at https://curl.se/docs/caextract.html do not change.
-CA_BUNDLE_DATE=2026-09-25
-CA_BUNDLE_SHA256=a41b5d356aea97a529fe27e0f7316d2f9d946d75927476cf9cf1b90637d00505
+CA_BUNDLE_DATE=2026-10-20
+CA_BUNDLE_SHA256=796f1389bfea13c0ed78f663b765baaff54a508e5483786bd6ece73c5e3e3cbe
 CA_BUNDLE_URL=https://curl.se/ca/cacert-$CA_BUNDLE_DATE.pem
 fail() { echo "build_tls_ps5: $*" >&2; exit 1; }
 while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
-- 
2.43.0

